Absolutely. Here is the **full optimized C++ version**. It uses a fixed 44-byte block header and a single 64-byte SHA-256 compression block, so it avoids allocating a `vector` for every nonce. The eight 32-bit regions map exactly onto the 256-bit digest.

The default difficulty is deliberately moderate (`4` zero bits in each region) so you can verify that it actually mines successfully. Increase the values afterward.

