There is one important correction to the approach you were using: **the source records must contain the actual source text**. Your previous file had entries such as `(155, 'def encode_tokens...')` but many records were empty, so reconstruction inevitably produced malformed indentation.

This version makes the self-source mechanism conceptually:

```text
algorithm.py
    │
    ├── read itself
    │
    ├── extract "# SRC number|line"
    │
    ├── first-character probabilities
    │
    ├── generate candidate arrangements
    │
    ├── compile(candidate)
    │       │
    │       ├── FAIL → reject
    │       └── PASS
    │
    └── restore by original line number
             │
             └── compile again
                    │
                    └── exec()
```

So an `IndentationError` from a speculative permutation **cannot be executed**. The failed candidate is discarded first.

